# Core instructions

- Read `README.md`, `CONTRIBUTING.md`, and the relevant source before editing. Make focused changes and reuse existing helpers.
- This repository publishes optional SNMP data and its compiler. Curated offline seed profiles, polling, tenant imports, and UI behavior belong to the Kaleidoscope platform.
- Keep hand-authored profiles, generated dictionaries, identity registry entries, and raw MIB sources distinct. A dictionary must never become an automatically assigned polling profile.
- Treat schemas and validation code as the implemented local contract; reconcile changes with `docs/FORMAT.md` and examples. Report disagreements rather than assuming documentation proves implementation.
- Use Node 22+ and pnpm 9, matching CI. Run package commands from `tools/`; there is no root workspace, build, lint, database, or deployment command.
- Search `tools/`, `schema/`, and the relevant vendor directory first. Avoid reading the entire MIB or generated JSON corpus into context.
- Do not invent device testing, successful commands, imported behavior, or library capabilities. Separate observed results from assumptions.
- If delegating work, pass the task boundaries and applicable rules to the agent; do not assume it inherited them. Coordinate ownership of shared files.
- Keep credentials, SNMP community strings, customer identifiers, private walks, and machine-specific connector settings out of this public repository. Preserve vendor copyright and license notices.
